# --- Unemployed OS: AUR access behind the Software Center (Part I) ---
git
base-devel
# sassc: not for end users -- customize_airootfs.sh's install_extension()
# runs `make install` on dash-to-dock at ISO-build time, and its Makefile
# compiles stylesheet.css via sassc. Without it, that recursive make step
# fails (Error 127) but the outer `make install` target still returns 0,
# so the failure was silent: no error surfaced, but dash-to-dock never
# actually got copied into /usr/share/gnome-shell/extensions -- caught by
# a real boot test where the extension directory was simply missing.
sassc

# --- Unemployed OS: Windows compatibility layer (Part IV) ---
# wine needs [multilib] enabled (see pacman.conf) for real 32-bit Windows
# app/game support -- without it this silently only covers 64-bit apps.
# vkd3d translates Direct3D 12 calls into Vulkan. DXVK (the same idea for
# D3D9/10/11) is NOT in any repo enabled here -- dxvk-bin is AUR-only
# (mkarchiso can't build AUR packages) and [cachyos] ships dxvk-mingw-git
# instead, which needs a mingw toolchain (not appropriate for the base
# image). This build-broke the ISO ("target not found: dxvk-bin") until
# caught by review + an actual build attempt. winetricks can install
# DXVK into a wine prefix post-install (`winetricks dxvk`) as the
# practical workaround until a real repo-provided package exists.
wine
winetricks
vkd3d

